{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-04T07:31:46.947Z","author":"pm-github","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"ci","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"Observed on open [PR56](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/pull/56), head `8805e866f7a55e1ac48f8b7ab9ab7979fca593e0`, rechecked current on 2026-11-03 at 20:05 UTC. The PR upgrades development SDK 10.28 →10.30 without changing repair implementation or tests.\n\n## Hosted evidence\n[Node 22](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/actions/runs/41706993031/job/126164822295) and [Node 26](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/actions/runs/41706993031/job/126164823666) each report 189 tests, 187 passed, 2 failed:\n- [repair-model.test.ts 58](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/blob/8805e866f7a55e1ac48f8b7ab9ab7979fca593e0/test/repair-model.test.ts#L58): sequence 0 fails deep equality after JSON round-trip because the SDK receipt contains optional `undefined` author_source/source_kind/note properties that JSON omits.\n- [repairs.test.ts 49](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/blob/8805e866f7a55e1ac48f8b7ab9ab7979fca593e0/test/repairs.test.ts#L49): repeating an unchanged revision-bound preview fails equality because `validation.records[].after.metadata.updated_at` differs between fresh staged validations.\n\n## Cause and goal\n[buildRepairPreview](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/blob/8805e866f7a55e1ac48f8b7ab9ab7979fca593e0/src/repairs.ts#L177) forwards the entire `previewItemMutations` validation result into its public receipt. The host's [staged-record API addition](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1598) means that result now includes normalized staged records, not just the earlier validation summary.\n\nThe closed [authoring-repair feature](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/blob/8805e866f7a55e1ac48f8b7ab9ab7979fca593e0/.agents/pm/features/pm-lint-authoring-repair-previews.toon) records SDK/JSON/TOON replay and 500-sequence evidence. The tests explicitly require serializable round-trip equality and unchanged-revision receipt equality. Actual newly forwarded optional properties and staged timestamps violate those existing comparisons. Stable plan identity and a fresh validation payload need an explicit compatibility contract rather than silently treating the candidate as certified.\n\n## Independent bounded check\nExecuted the exact current `buildRepairPreview` body under Node 24.22.1 with wholly synthetic SDK dependencies and two synthetic staged validation results. Revision, plan_key and repair patch stayed identical, while the different staged timestamp and optional undefined field were forwarded unchanged. This isolates the forwarding behavior; it is not a real SDK integration rerun. The hosted Node 22/26 jobs provide the real dependency evidence.\n\n## Acceptance and limits\nDefine which receipt fields are stable replay identity and which are freshly staged validation evidence, preserving the host's native semantics. Ensure SDK/JSON/TOON consumers have an explicit comparable representation for optional fields, and update implementation/tests consistently with that documented contract. Keep stale-revision refusal, zero source-byte changes, independent SDK readback, native metadata preservation and all 500 sequences at unchanged coverage thresholds. Rerun Node 22/26 and packed acceptance on the final head.\n\nThis report does not establish source tracker mutation, an invalid mechanical patch or a core staged-record defect. It establishes two current upgrade acceptance failures and their receipt-shape cause. All 56 all-status GitHub issues/PRs, current PR56 discussion and all current canonical tracker records were checked. The closed repair feature supplies the goal; no existing record owns these SDK 10.30 compatibility failures. No installs, provider requests or external mutations were performed during the independent check."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-lint-github-253a36d6af64-57"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"SDK 2026.10.30 upgrade breaks repair-preview transport and replay equality"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH issue #57: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/issues/57 · author @unbraind · created 2026-11-03T20:09:10Z · updated 2026-11-03T20:09:10Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["gh:unbraind/pm-lint#57","github_author:unbraind"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-04T07:31:46.947Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-04T07:31:46.947Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pm-github"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"2a84c3a6ea869c62b07d7b1355ea024137934ede3f51218670658b8f912b1994","item_hash_version":3,"message":"pm-github import create unbraind/pm-lint#57","event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"97f267713145cc208bb7a78deffd88e0ec33ceecf022076c1e5e524abf063f77"}
